        title = 'UNT Physics Colloquium Presents Dr. Juejun (JJ) Hu',
        description = 'Title: Metasurfaces Beyond Flatland: From Planar Optics to Curved and Panoramic Systems

 

Abstract: Metasurfaces are redefining how optical systems are designed by enabling precise wavefront control in ultrathin, lightweight form factors. In this talk, I will highlight our efforts to push metasurface optics beyond conventional narrow-angle, small-depth regimes toward wide-angle, large depth-of-field (DOF), and conformal operation. I will discuss how metasurface-based architectures can support panoramic and wide-angle imaging, how optical and computational co-design can extend DOF and system robustness, and how scalable manufacturing approaches allow metasurfaces to be integrated onto curved and unconventional substrates. These advances point toward a new generation of compact, multifunctional optical systems that break free from the geometric and form-factor constraints of traditional refractive optics.',
