    INSERT INTO events (
        title,
        description,
        location_id,
        start_date_time,
        end_date_time,
        event_type,
        status
    )
    SELECT
        'UNT Friends of the Humanities Talk',
        'Dr. Anaïs Faurt
Assistant Professor of
History,
Chestnut Hill College

Minor Problems: Young Insurgents and the Politics of Childhood in France’s Wars of Decolonization (1945-1962)

 

After World War II, the child became a vulnerable figure to protect and rehabilitate in Europe. At the same time, however, France brutally repressed anticolonial nationalist insurrections in the then-French territories of Vietnam (1945-1954) and Algeria (1954-1962). Decolonization politicized indigenous childhood. Children and youths actively participated in anti-colonial movements. Boys and girls acted as informants, messengers, and suppliers. They cooked food, distributed water, and buried weapons in their backyards. Some anonymously blackmailed colonial officials, some threw small rocks at their faces, and others ran and hid. Children set off explosives. They killed. Courts and child welfare authorities were presented with a conundrum: were these young people still innocent, unwittingly corrupted by anti-colonial nationalist groups or were they beyond saving? This talk will examines how colonial bureaucrats sought to distinguish between rebellious children and dangerous insurgents at the collapse of empire.',
        (SELECT location_id FROM resolved_location),
        TIMESTAMP '2026-04-02 15:45:00',
        TIMESTAMP '2026-04-03 04:45:00',
        'Lectures & Speakers',
        'SCHEDULED'::event_status
    WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM existing_event)
    RETURNING event_id
),
