Having a clear and identifiable personal brand can help new-career designers, visual artists, entrepreneurs, and others communicate their personality, style, and sense of identity to new customers, clients, and employers – all without the use of words or long-winded mission statements! 

 

Course Description 

Learn aspects of digital design in order to create visually unique logos, portfolios, websites, and visual language. Software covered include Adobe Illustrator, Adobe Photoshop, and Framer, among others. 

 

Course Goals and Objectives 

By the end of this course, students will be able to: 

- Understand basic elements of visual design, 

- Apply their understanding in digital design software to create graphics, and 

