Ever wondered what it’s really like to work on a research team? Join us for an engaging panel discussion featuring both undergraduate and graduate students who have collaborated with faculty and peers on research projects. Hear firsthand about the challenges, successes, and lessons learned when working in diverse, collaborative environments - and discover strategies to thrive in your own research teams. This workshop is open to both undergraduate and graduate students.

 

What You’ll Gain:

Insights into the dynamics of working with faculty and other student researchersTips for effective communication and conflict resolution in team settingsStrategies for balancing roles, responsibilities, and expectationsAdvice on building strong professional relationships and networksReal stories about what makes collaboration rewarding—and what to watch out forInteractive Component:
